msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1543 
msgid "Creates a JSON array using list of values [\"john\", \"arun\"]."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1541 
msgid ""
"Creates a JSON object with key as \"name\" and value as [\"john\", "
"\"arun\"]."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5153 
msgid ""
"Creates a chart for a statistical aggregation applied to a field against "
"time. When \\\n"
"the data is split by a field, each distinct value of this split-by field "
"is a series. \\\n"
"If used with an eval-expression, the split-by-clause is required. \\p\\\\"
"\n"
"When a where clause is not provided, you can use limit and agg options to"
" specify \\\n"
"series filtering. If limit=0, there is no series filtering. \\p\\\\\n"
"When specifying multiple data series with a split-by-clause, you can use "
"sep and \\\n"
"format options to construct output field names.\\p\\\\\n"
"When called without any bin-options, timechart defaults to bins=300. This"
" finds \\\n"
"the smallest bucket size that results in no more than three hundred "
"distinct buckets."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:2814 
msgid ""
"Creates a single event where the value for the 'data' field is a single "
"JSON array that includes a series of JSON objects."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:2809 
msgid ""
"Creates a specified number of empty search results. This command will run"
" only on the local machine \\\n"
"by default and will generate one unannotated empty result. It maybe used "
"in conjunction with the eval command to \\\n"
"generate an empty result for the eval command to operate on. \\\n"
"Events can also be generated from inlined CSV/JSON strings via the "
"provided 'format' and 'data' arguments."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:799 
msgid ""
"Creates a table of statistics suitable for charting.  Whereas timechart "
"generates a \\\n"
"chart with _time as the x-axis, chart lets you select an arbitrary field "
"as the \\\n"
"x-axis with the \"by\" or \"over\" keyword. If necessary, the x-axis "
"field is converted \\\n"
"to discrete numerical quantities.\\p\\\\\n"
"When chart includes a split-by-clause, the columns in the output table "
"represents a \\\n"
"distinct value of the split-by-field. (With stats, each row represents a "
"single \\\n"
"unique combination of values of the group-by-field. The table displays "
"ten columns \\\n"
"by default, but you can specify a where clause to adjust the number of "
"columns.\\p\\\\\n"
"When a where clause is not provided, you can use limit and agg options to"
" specify \\\n"
"series filtering. If limit=0, there is no series filtering.  \\p\\\\\n"
"The limit option start with \"top\" or \"bottom\" to determine which "
"series to select.  \\\n"
"A number without a prefix means the same thing as starting with top.  "
"Default is 10. \\p\\\\\n"
"When specifying multiple data series with a split-by-clause, you can use "
"sep and \\\n"
"format options to construct output field names."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5144 
msgid "Creates a time series chart with corresponding table of statistics."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:6278 
msgid ""
"Creates one or more relative time fields and adds them to returned "
"events. The added fields have human-readable time values such as \"5 days"
" ago\", \"1 minute ago\", and \"2 years ago\"."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:6297 
msgid ""
"Creates one or more relative time fields and adds them to returned "
"events. \\\n"
"Each relative time field provides a human-readable value of the "
"difference \\\n"
"between 'now' and a value of \"timefield\". Human-readable values look "
"like \\\n"
"\"5 days ago\", \"1 minute ago\", and \"2 years ago\". If no arguments "
"are provided, \\\n"
"reltime adds a relative time field named 'reltime' to each event. The "
"value \\\n"
"of 'reltime' in this case is the difference between 'now' and '_time'. "
"\\p\\\\\n"
"Arguments: \\\n"
"\"timefield\": A field in the event data with a valid timestamp value. "
"You can \\\n"
"provide multiple time fields as a comma-separated list bounded by double "
"\\\n"
"quotation marks. If the \"timefield\" argument specifies only one time "
"field, \\\n"
"reltime adds a relative time field named 'reltime' to the returned "
"events, \\\n"
"where the value of 'reltime' is the difference between 'now' and the \\\n"
"specified time field. When \"timefield\" specifies multiple time fields, "
"\\\n"
"reltime creates relative time fields with the \"timefield\" field names, "
"\\\n"
"prefixed by the string set by \"prefix\". \\p\\\\\n"
"\"prefix\": Sets a prefix string for relative time fields when you "
"specify \\\n"
"multiple time fields for \"timefield\". When you specify multiple values "
"\\\n"
"for \"timefield\" and you do not set a \"prefix\" string, reltime uses "
"'reltime_' \\\n"
"as a default prefix."
msgstr ""

