#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:2211 
msgid ""
"Returns information about the buckets in the Splunk Enterprise index. \\\n"
"The Splunk Enterprise index is the repository for data from Splunk "
"Enterprise. \\\n"
"As incoming data is indexed, or transformed into events, Splunk "
"Enterprise \\\n"
"creates files of rawdata and metadata (index files). The files reside in "
"sets \\\n"
"of directories organized by age. These directories are called buckets. \\"
"\n"
"When invoked without the bin-span option, information about the buckets "
"\\\n"
"is returned in the following fields: \\\n"
"bucketId, endEpoch, eventCount, guID, hostCount, id, index, modTime, "
"path, \\\n"
"rawSize, sizeOnDiskMB, sourceCount, sourceTypeCount, splunk_server, "
"startEpoch, state, \\\n"
"corruptReason. The corruptReason field only appears when "
"corruptonly=true. \\p\\\\\n"
"When invoked with a bin span, a table of the spans of each bucket is "
"returned."
msgstr ""

