msgid ""
"Takes a UTC time as the first argument and a relative time specifier as "
"the second argument and returns the UTC time of that relative time "
"applied to the first arugment."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1461 
msgid ""
"Takes a UTC time as the first argument and renders it as a string using "
"the format specified by the second argument"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1409 
msgid ""
"Takes a field argument, returning the number of values if the field is "
"multivalued, one if the field is single valued and has a value, and null "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1483 
msgid ""
"Takes a multivalued field as input and returns a multivalued field with "
"its duplicate values removed"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1485 
msgid ""
"Takes a multivalued field as input and returns a multivalued field with "
"its values sorted lexicographically"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1569 
msgid ""
"Takes a non-negative integer as argument and inverts every bit in the "
"binary representation of the number. It also takes an optional second "
"argument with a default value of (2,53)-1. Both arguments are restricted "
"to be in the range [0, (2^53 -1)], a failure of which returns NULL."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1369 
msgid "Takes a number and returns its absolute value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1397 
msgid "Takes a number and returns its natural log."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1379 
msgid ""
"Takes a number as its argument, and returns the exact value of the result"
" without truncating for significant figures or precision. Uses double "
"precision."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1381 
msgid "Takes a number x and returns e^x."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1385 
msgid "Takes a number x and returns the floor of x, which in this example is 1."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1463 
msgid ""
"Takes a string time representing and parses it using the format specified"
" by the second argument, returning a UTC time"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1553 
msgid ""
"Takes a value \"occupations\" and returns the value if it can be parsed "
"as JSON. Otherwise, the function returns null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1405 
msgid ""
"Takes an arbitrary number of number and string arguments and returns the "
"max, with strings being greater than numbers. So this example will return"
" either \"foo\" or field, depending on the value of field. The "
"corresponding min function also exists."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1455 
msgid ""
"Takes an even number of arguments like case(), with odd arguments being "
"boolean expressions. The even arguments are strings, and the function "
"returns the string corresponding to the first expression that evaluates "
"to false, or null if all checks pass. The example runs a simple check for"
" valid ports."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1371 
msgid ""
"Takes an even number of arguments with arguments 1,3,5, etc. being "
"boolean expressions. The function returns the argument following the "
"first expression that evaluates to true, defaulting to NULL if none are "
"true."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1377 
msgid ""
"Takes any number of arguments and returns the first value that is not "
"null. The ifnull function does the exact same thing, so both names are "
"acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1399 
msgid ""
"Takes either one or two numeric arguments, returning the log of the first"
" argument using the base provided by the second argument, in this case "
"log of number base 2. The default base is 10 if the second argument is "
"omitted."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1443 
msgid ""
"Takes either two or three arguments - the first is a string and the last "
"two are numeric. The function returns a substring of the first argument "
"starting at the index specified by the second argument with the number of"
" characters specified by the third. If a third argument is not given, it "
"returns the rest of the string. The indexes follow SQLite semantics in "
"that they start at 1 and negative indices can be used, which start from "
"the end of the string. The example concatenates \"str\" and \"ing\" "
"together, returning \"string\""
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1419 
msgid ""
"Takes no arguments and returns null, which is how the evaluation engine "
"represents no value. Setting a field to null will clear its value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1417 
msgid ""
"Takes no arguments and returns the time that the search was started, in "
"unix time (seconds since epoch)."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1423 
msgid "Takes no arguments, returning the pi constant to 11 digits of precision."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1427 
msgid "Takes no arguments, returns a pseudo-random number."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1581 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is a double. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isbool()' for booleans,'isnum()' for "
"numbers, 'isint()' for integers, 'isstr()' for strings, 'ismv()' for "
"multivalues, 'isarray()' for arrays, 'isobject()' for objects, and "
"'isnull()' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1587 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is a multivalue. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isbool' for booleans,'isnum' for numbers, "
"'isdouble' for doubles, 'isint' for integers, 'isstr' for strings, "
"'isarray' for arrays, 'isobject' for objects, and 'isnull' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1579 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is a number. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isbool' for booleans, 'isdouble' for "
"doubles, 'isint' for integers, 'isstr' for strings, 'ismv' for "
"multivalues, 'isarray' for arrays, 'isobject' for objects, and 'isnull' "
"for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1585 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is a string. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isbool()' for booleans,'isnum()' for "
"numbers, 'isdouble()' for doubles, 'isint()' for integers, 'ismv()' for "
"multivalues, 'isarray()' for arrays, 'isobject()' for objects, and "
"'isnull()' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1577 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is an array (i.e."
" \"[1, 2, 3]\"). Corresponding functions are: 'isbool' for booleans, "
"'isnum' for numbers, 'isdouble' for doubles, 'isint' for integers, "
"'isstr' for strings, 'ismv' for multivalues, 'isobject' for objects, and "
"'isnull' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1583 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is an integer. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isbool' for booleans,'isnum' for numbers, "
"'isdouble' for doubles, 'isstr' for strings, 'ismv' for multivalues, "
"'isarray' for arrays, 'isobject' for objects, and 'isnull' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1589 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is an object. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isbool' for booleans,'isnum' for numbers, "
"'isdouble' for doubles, 'isint' for integers, 'isstr' for strings, 'ismv'"
" for multivalues, 'isarray' for arrays, and 'isnull' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1389 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns \"true\" if the argument is boolean. "
"Corresponding functions are: 'isnum' for numbers, 'isdouble' for doubles,"
" 'isint' for integers, 'isstr' for strings, 'ismv' for multivalues, "
"'isarray' for arrays, 'isobject' for objects, and 'isnull' for null."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1451 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns a string representation of its type. The "
"example result is NumberStringBoolInvalid."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1601 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns the equivalent array value of the field, "
"if any."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1591 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns the equivalent boolean value of the field,"
" if any."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1599 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns the equivalent multivalue value of the "
"field, if any."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1603 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument and returns the equivalent object value of the field, "
"if any."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1413 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument which is a boolean expression that references EXACTLY "
"one field. It returns that multivalued field filtered by the given "
"expression, so this example will return all values of the field email "
"that end in .net or .org."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1391 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument, returning true iff the field is not null. A useful "
"check for whether the field contains a value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1433 
msgid ""
"Takes one argument, which is a search string. The function returns true "
"iff the event matches the search string."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1441 
msgid ""
"Takes one numeric argument and returns its square root, in this example "
"it would be 3."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1595 
msgid ""
"Takes one or two arguments and returns the equivalent double value of the"
" field, if any. The second argument specifies the numeric base used to "
"convert strings."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1593 
msgid ""
"Takes one or two arguments and returns the equivalent integer value of "
"the field, if any. The second argument specifies the numeric base used to"
" convert strings."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1597 
msgid ""
"Takes one or two arguments and returns the equivalent number value of the"
" field, if any. The second argument specifies the numeric base used to "
"convert strings."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1445 
msgid ""
"Takes one or two arguments, returning a string representation of the "
"first argument with optional formatting for numbers. For numbers you can "
"specify \"hex\" or \"commas\" as a second argument to format the number "
"accordingly. The return value for this example is \"True 0xF 12,345.68\"."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1431 
msgid ""
"Takes one or two numeric arguments, returning the first argument rounded "
"to the amount of decimal places specified by the second. The default is "
"to round to an integer, so the example would return 4. round(2.555, 2) "
"would return 2.56."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1447 
msgid ""
"Takes one or two string arguments, and returns the first string with the "
"characters in the second argument trimmed from both sides. If no second "
"argument is specified, spaces and tabs are trimmed. This example returns "
"\"abc\". There are also ltrim and rtrim functions for trimming only the "
"left and right sides, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1407 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument and returns its md5 hash value as a string, in "
"this case returning the hash of field's value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1435 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument and returns its sha1 hash value based on the "
"FIPS compliant SHA-1 hash function as a string, in this case returning "
"the hash of field's value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1437 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument and returns its sha256 hash value based on the "
"FIPS compliant SHA-256 hash function as a string, in this case returning "
"the hash of field's value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1439 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument and returns its sha512 hash value based on the "
"FIPS compliant SHA-512 hash function as a string, in this case returning "
"the hash of field's value."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1401 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument and returns the lowercase version, in this "
"example lowercasing the value provided by the field username. The upper "
"function also exists for returning the uppercase version."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1453 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument and returns the url decoded. The example result"
" is \"http://www.splunk.com/download?r=header\"."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1393 
msgid ""
"Takes one string argument, returning the length of the string. In this "
"example it would return the length of the string in field."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5942 
msgid ""
"Takes previous search results, and produces a list of promising searches "
"that may be used as event-types."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:6398 
msgid ""
"Takes previous search results, and produces a list of\\\n"
"promising searches that may be used as event types.  Returns up to MAX\\\n"
"event types, defaulting to 10.  If the \"notcovered\" keyword is\\\n"
"specified, then event types that are already covered by other\\\n"
"eventtypes are not returned.  At most 5000 events are analyzed for\\\n"
"discovering event types.  If the \"useraw\" keyword is specified, then\\\n"
"phrases in the _raw text of the events is used for generating event\\\n"
"types."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1823 
msgid "Takes the results of a subsearch and formats them into a single result."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1429 
msgid ""
"Takes three arguments - replace(input_string, regex_pattern_to_replace, "
"replacement_string) returns the input string with all instances of the "
"regex pattern replaced with the replacement string. You can also include "
"matched groups in the third argument by escaping the group number "
"matched. The example returns date with the month and day numbers "
"switched, so if the input was 1/12/2009 the return value would be "
"12/1/2009."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1387 
msgid ""
"Takes three arguments, the first being a boolean expression. The function"
" returns the second argument if it evaluates to true, and the third "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1421 
msgid ""
"Takes two arguments, returning the first argument if the arguments are "
"different, and null otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1375 
msgid ""
"Takes two arguments, the first being the subnet to match and the second "
"being an ip address. This boolean function returns true if the ip matches"
" the valid subnet, or false otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1425 
msgid "Takes two numeric arguments, returning x^y"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1563 
msgid ""
"Takes two or more non-negative integers as arguments and performs logical"
" bitwise and on them"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1565 
msgid ""
"Takes two or more non-negative integers as arguments and performs logical"
" bitwise or on them"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1567 
msgid ""
"Takes two or more non-negative integers as arguments and performs logical"
" bitwise xor on them"
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1411 
msgid ""
"Takes two or three arguments, the first being a field and the second two "
"being numbers, which returns a subset of the multivalued field using the "
"indexes provided. For mvindex(mvfield, startindex, [endindex]) endindex "
"is inclusive and optional. Both start and endindex can be negative, where"
" -1 = last element, and if endindex is not specified, it returns just the"
" value at startindex. If the indexes are out of range or invalid, the "
"result is null. Since indexes start at zero, this example returns the "
"third value in multifield if it exists."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1403 
msgid ""
"Takes two string arguments, and returns true iff the first argument "
"matches the regex provided by the second argument. This example returns "
"true iff field matches the basic pattern of an ip address. Note that the "
"example used ^ and $ to perform a full match."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1395 
msgid ""
"Takes two string arguments, returning true iff the first argument is like"
" the SQLite pattern in the second argument. This example returns true if "
"the field value starts with foo."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1555 
msgid ""
"Takes two valid IPv4 addresses as arguments. The first argument is an IP "
"mask, and the second is an IP address. This function generates a new "
"masked IP address by applying the mask to the IP address through a "
"bitwise AND operation. You can use this function to simplify isolation of"
" an octet without splitting the given IP address. A valid IPv4 address is"
" a quad-dotted notation of four decimal integers, each ranging from 0 to "
"255."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1559 
msgid ""
"Takes two valid non negative integers as arguments. The first argument is"
" a value and the second the amount it must be shifted left by. Both "
"arguments are restricted to be in the range [0, (2^53 -1)], a failure of "
"which returns NULL. All answers are masked to stay below the (2^53 -1) "
"limit in the event of overflows. Shifting left drops the 53rd bit and "
"appends a 0 to the binary representation of the input."
msgstr ""

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1561 
msgid ""
"Takes two valid non negative integers as arguments. The first argument is"
" a value and the second the amount it must be shifted right by. Both "
"arguments are restricted to be in the range [0, (2^53 -1)], a failure of "
"which returns NULL. All answers are masked to stay below the (2^53 -1) "
"limit in the event of overflows. Shifting right drops the rightmost bit "
"and prepends a 0 to the binary representation of the input."
msgstr ""

